# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# Applied by the assets layer to every static response (HTML, JS, CSS, images). /api/* is answered by the Worker first
# (wrangler.jsonc run_worker_first) and sets its own headers in worker/http.ts, so nothing here touches the API.
# The CSP is deliberately only the SAFE subset: no default-src / script-src / connect-src, because the site ships inline
# Astro island bootstraps, viem calls the public chain RPC, and the Google site-verification meta must keep working.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'

# Caching. Hashed build output and the self-hosted fonts never change under the same URL, so they are cached for a year and
# never revalidated. Images keep their names but rarely change: a week, and a day of stale-while-revalidate. HTML is left on the
# default (always revalidated, answered with an ETag), so a new deploy shows up on the next visit.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
